WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Count every commandment in
the Torah, as the rabbis did,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.230
and you reach 613.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.010
248 tell you what to do.

4
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.300
365 tell you what not to do.

5
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.880
Yet only ten were written
on two tablets of stone.

6
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.690
The Torah has its own name
for them: the ten words.

7
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:25.860
So if there are 613 commandments, why
did only ten go on the stone tablets?

8
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.300
In this mission, you'll see
how Jews sort the commandments:

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.600
some towards God, some
towards other people.

10
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:38.110
Then you'll compare how Orthodox, Reform
and Hasidic Jews keep the mitzvot today.

11
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.800
Your mission: find out why only ten of
the 613 commandments went on the stone

12
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.590
tablets.
